+/// Exit code reported when Windows output capture failed and the command itself exited with 0.
+///
+/// The partial output captured before the failure is still returned. 253 avoids the codes that
+/// shells, `timeout` and Codex assign meaning to: 124 (timeout), 125-127 (`timeout`/shell launch
+/// failures), 128-192 (128 + signal) and 255 (generic failure and `-1` wrapped to a byte). When
+/// the command's own exit code is already non-zero, that code is kept: it is the more specific
+/// failure information, and the capture failure is still reported through the diagnostic and
+/// `SandboxErr::Capture`.
+const EXEC_OUTPUT_TRUNCATED_EXIT_CODE: i32 = 253;
